  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has long, slender leaves that release a pleasant fragrance when crushed, making it a great addition to sensory gardens. Its weeping branches create a graceful, cascading effect that can be used to teach about plant form and structure. The small, white flowers appear in clusters and can be utilized in lessons about pollination and seasonal changes. The tree&#x27;s resilience to coastal conditions makes it a useful example for discussing plant adaptations to different environments.",
